    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0181" n="1015" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1015"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/6557</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Diplomatic and Consular Officers in All
                            Countries
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-29T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Note and advise consular officers your jurisdiction that War Trade Board has
                    granted general license authorizing trans-shipment in United States ports of all
                    goods destined for Mexican, Central American and South American ports, which
                    have been allowed to go forward by British, French or Italian authorities, even
                    though consignees are on enemy trading list.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
